% Test cases for the TEJSD policy (tejsd.le): synthetic claims for E0762 and
% A4465, fully documented, each concluding nothing at the question — the LCD
% denies the device as not reasonable and necessary whatever the record
% shows — and one decision of the Medicare Appeals Council (BioniCare
% Medical Technologies, 2009) transcribed as the customs rulings are: each
% fact quotes its passage, the Council's outcome is in the comment, not a
% fact.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base tejsd cases includes these resources:
    tejsd.

the knowledge base tejsd cases includes:

Council decision bionicare is published at "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/static/dab/decisions/council-decisions/bionicare.pdf".
the text of Council decision bionicare is at "sources/council/bionicare.txt".

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month rental claim for a TEJSD (E0762) at home, with the
% standard written order, the delivery and its proof: within the benefit,
% not reasonable and necessary, and no change to the record makes it
% payable. The stage names the remedy, not the question: "the query fails
% at which section" blames the earliest section holding a rule the attempt
% tried and could not prove, and this policy has no rule at all for the
% question — the payable rule of dmepos.le, in the remedy, is the first that
% fails.
scenario device_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the joint stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the joint stimulator is "E0762".
    the joint stimulator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the order for the joint stimulator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the joint stimulator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the joint stimulator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the joint stimulator includes order date.
    the order for the joint stimulator includes description of the item.
    the order for the joint stimulator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the joint stimulator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the joint stimulator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the joint stimulator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the joint stimulator.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [].

% The same device furnished in a skilled nursing facility: statutorily
% non-covered (Policy Article A52713) — the claim fails at applicability,
% before the question is reached.
scenario nursing_facility is:
    claim 1 is for the joint stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the joint stimulator is "E0762".
    the joint stimulator is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is skilled nursing facility.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A replacement wrap (A4465) for the device: a supply of a device no rule
% covers (the stage as in device_complete).
scenario replacement_wrap is:
    claim 1 is for the electrode wrap.
    the HCPCS code of the electrode wrap is "A4465".
    the electrode wrap is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% A fourth rental month with continued need and use documented: the
% continued-coverage record of dmepos.le is met, the question still is not
% (the stage as in device_complete).
scenario month_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the joint stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the joint stimulator is "E0762".
    the joint stimulator is furnished to Dee.
    the residence of Dee is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the medical record documents continued need for the joint stimulator on 2026-05-20.
    the record documents continued use of the joint stimulator on 2026-05-20.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Council: not covered — "the Council adopts the ALJ's ultimate conclusion
% that Medicare coverage is not warranted for the BIO-1000 devices and
% related supplies furnished to the beneficiaries", the device not having
% been shown reasonable and necessary for osteoarthritis of the knee. The
% decision names no residence; the model, wanting one, fails at
% applicability rather than at the question — the same outcome, one step
% earlier. The Council's finding ("The Council finds that the evidence, as
% summarized below, does not establish that, at the time the devices were
% furnished in 2004 and 2005, the BIO-1000 met medical necessity standards
% for Medicare coverage") is not recorded as a fact: no rule of this policy
% reads a finding, what the Council decided case by case being what the LCD
% now denies by rule.
scenario bionicare is, as stated in Council decision bionicare:
    claim 1 is for the BIO-1000,
        confer "the appellant billed Medicare for the rental of the BIO-1000 under HCPCS code E0762".
    the HCPCS code of the BIO-1000 is "E0762",
        confer "the appellant billed Medicare for the rental of the BIO-1000 under HCPCS code E0762".
    the BIO-1000 is furnished to beneficiary one,
        confer "a device that delivers pulsed electrical stimulation to the knee and is used in the treatment of osteoarthritis of the knee".
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1,
        confer "the appellant billed Medicare for the rental of the BIO-1000 under HCPCS code E0762".
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2004-06-01,
        confer "which the appellant rented to 47 beneficiaries on various dates in 2004 and 2005".
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
